From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elkir0 <elkir0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/24] ARM: gts28ltexx: scheduler and timer tuning; audio,
 sensors, battery in the board

Kernel tuning (gts28ltexx_defconfig), asked for by the Omarchy work:
HZ_250, PREEMPT, NO_HZ_IDLE, HIGH_RES_TIMERS, SCHED_MC and MGLRU, with
capacity-dmips-mhz from the vendor kernel (A53 2048, A57 3575,
kernel_universal5433 arch/arm/kernel/topology.c:72-78) so the scheduler
tells the clusters apart.  RTC_SYSTOHC is off: Android keeps its own
reference on the RTC.

The milestone fragments move into the board file and the defconfig:
- section 15, audio (exynos5433-gts28ltexx-audio.dtsi, was -m6.dtsi):
  WM1814 on HSI2C3, I2S0, the gts28-wm1814 card; sound core, Arizona,
  the codec, I2S, PL330 and the card driver are modules;
- section 16, sensors (exynos5433-gts28ltexx-sensors.dtsi, was
  -m7.dtsi): LSM6DS3 and YAS537 on HSI2C10 (their drivers now modules),
  the cover Hall switch as gpio-keys SW_LID;
- section 17, battery (exynos5433-gts28ltexx-battery.dtsi): the SM5703
  fuel gauge on HSI2C7; POWER_SUPPLY on, the driver a module.
The -m6/-m7 wrappers and their config fragments are removed.

Checked on the SM-T715 (same build): timer resolution 1 ns, CPU
capacities 586/1024, no vblank timeout, Phosh, Wi-Fi and Bluetooth up;
speaker-to-microphone loopback at 1 kHz; battery 99 % in UPower;
gyroscope and YAS537 readable, iio-sensor-proxy sees the accelerometer;
hall-sensor watched by logind; no failed unit, no kernel warning.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
